---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LeadBlock from '../components/LeadBlock.astro';
---
<Base title="How Online A-level Tutoring Works | Booking and Lessons | aleveltutors.online" description="How our online A-level lessons work: booking, your first lesson, recorded lessons, resources and payment after each lesson.">
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">How it works</div>
      <h1>How online lessons work</h1>
      <p>People learn best from people. Our lessons put an experienced teacher and the right exam questions in front of you, with nothing getting in the way.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Booking</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><h3>Get in touch</h3><p>WhatsApp or the enquiry form: subject, exam board, year group, and the two times that suit you best.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Agree a time</h3><p>We match you with the specialist for your board. Most students choose a regular weekly slot.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Secure the booking</h3><p>A card secures the booking. It is charged after each lesson, not in advance.</p></li>
        <li><h3>First contact</h3><p>Your tutor gets in touch before the first lesson to explain what to expect and ask which topics you want to cover.</p></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:18px">You’ll get automatic reminders before lessons. You can move a lesson, and if your circumstances change you can stop.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="block alt">
    <div class="wrap features">
      <div><h3>Technology that just works</h3><p>Lessons run on Zoom or Google Meet with good audio and video, using tools we have tested, so the lesson is about the subject, not the technology.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Shared screen, live annotation</h3><p>You and your tutor see the same slides, diagrams and exam questions and can both write on them as you work.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Recorded lessons</h3><p>Every lesson is recorded and kept in a private online archive, so you can watch any explanation again when you revise.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Resources and questions</h3><p>Pre-lesson materials, annotated notes and exam questions are kept together. Send in questions you got stuck on and your tutor will go through them.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Learn from anywhere</h3><p>Lessons start as soon as you log on, from your usual desk, on holiday or after a move.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Free revision between lessons</h3><p>Each subject has a free revision site with past-paper questions by topic, so you can practise what you covered.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <LeadBlock heading="Ready to start?" />
</Base>
